[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3037245346","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108279#issuecomment-3037245346","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108279","id":3037245346,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61CK-i","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-04T21:11:21Z","updated_at":"2025-07-04T21:11:21Z","body":"Why do you need the tiles to be initialised in a certain order? It seems like there could be various reasons why the engine might initialise tiles in different orders, such as for performance reasons. Based on the optional [`_update_cells`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/classes/class_tilemaplayer.html#class-tilemaplayer-private-method-update-cells) method's description, I am guessing Godot only renders changed tiles, and attempts to render them in approximately the order they were changed (but doesn't make any guarantees of this). I don't feel this can be a bug if the engine doesn't commit to a specific guaranteed order.",